<title>GERMANY: BASF 9-mo pre-tax profit up 8.8 pct.</title>
<headline>BASF 9-mo pre-tax profit up 8.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LUDWIGSHAFEN, Germany 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30 (in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     3,369   vs 3,096</p>
<p>Group sales (excluding petroleum</p>
<p>    and natural gas taxes)		   36,119  vs 35,117</p>
<p>    Group foreign sales			26,580  vs 25,588</p>
<p>    Group domestic sales		     9,539   vs 9,529</p>
<p>    Group personnel costs		    7,547   vs 7,171</p>
<p>    Group fixed asset investments	  2,302   vs 1,894</p>
<p>    Parent pre-tax profit		    1,701   vs 1,708</p>
<p>    Parent sales				 15,356  vs 16,308</p>
<p>    Parent foreign sales		     10,603  vs 10,890</p>
<p>    Parent domestic sales		    4,753   vs 5,418</p>
<p>    Parent personnel costs		   3,516   vs 3,469</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of German chemical company is BASF AG. Analysts predicted an average 11 percent rise in pre-tax profits ranging between 3.41 and 3.51 billion marks with sales, excluding taxes, ranging between 33.56 and 33.75 billion marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
